str subclass's instance's) value."] [62 1 "// kindFor is the kind of a str whose largest code point is mx, and whether it is ASCII."] [75 1 "// unicodeLayout is the layout of o's mirror: its kind, ASCII flag, compactness (an exact str), length, the data's"] [76 1 "// offset and the bytes it needs."] [105 1 "// storeUnit and loadUnit write and read the character i of a kind k buffer at p."] [129 1 "// writeUnicode writes a str's PyASCIIObject (and its compact or legacy part) and characters at a (the handle's"] [130 1 "// memory, zeroed); a str PyUnicode_New made keeps a copy of its characters to see what C writes."] [135 36 "// hash: -1, not computed"] [143 2 "// state.interned (queue 594: test_check_interned): SSTATE_INTERNED_IMMORTAL_STATIC for the static singletons (the"] [144 2 "// empty str and the latin-1 characters), SSTATE_INTERNED_MORTAL for a str sys.intern holds"] [145 51 "// a str PyUnicode_New makes for C to fill is none of them"] [168 1 "// syncStrFromC copies the characters C wrote into a new str's mirror to the pyi str."] [188 1 "// strMirror is the mirror of a str's handle (nil: not a str), synchronized from C."] [200 1 "// maxCharOf is PyUnicode_MAX_CHAR_VALUE of a str's mirror."] [213 1 "// kindName is unicode_kind_name."] [226 1 "// modifiable is unicode_check_modifiable: a str PyUnicode_New made that C alone holds, not hashed by Python."] [234 1 "// newUnicode is PyUnicode_New(size, maxchar): a str of size NUL characters whose mirror has maxchar's kind, a new"] [235 1 "// reference."] [260 1 "// fromUnits is _PyUnicode_FromUCS1/2/4: the str of n characters of kind k at p (its largest character checked as"] [261 1 "// PyUnicode_New checks it)."] [274 1 "// uwriter is a PyUnicodeWriter: the characters written so far (its C pointer a block of the world's own, so that a"] [275 1 "// cast to _PyUnicodeWriter names the same writer)."] [282 1 "// writeRunes appends a str's characters (or a part of them) to a writer."] [289 1 "// unicodeTable: the native